18: 
19: ## F02 author, envelope and existing contracts
20: 
21: Create one separate MANIFEST Artifact, GENERATED, LIVE, PROJECT access, run_id=null, produced_by=current unrevoked Owner principal. Current same-SID Host metadata and Owner-root authority are checked in the private maintenance path; they do not impersonate the original executor. Envelope contains: schema/version/kind, current author ID and Owner-root public binding, observed_at, operation_id, plan_hash (defined below), historical project/task/run/runtime/epoch/dispatch identity, every evidence path/size/digest, original native artifacts list, original frame/ACK/native/cost facts, inference premises, rule version, explicit limitations and derived FAILED observation. Raw historical subject IDs/hashes are inside the envelope. Outer input_refs contains exactly the immutable profile Artifact VersionRef, source_refs=[], preventing the newly changed Run version from making the proof stale. Verify profile access is PROJECT and effective for this exact plan; a protected/stale profile is outside v1.
22: 
23: Do not call recoverArtifact: its author and use records belong to the old executor. Do not call serverArtifactMode: it emits OBSERVED. Do not append the new MANIFEST to old result_artifact_ids or the native output list. `run_id=null` means runtime_uploads, artifact_uses and artifact_use_proofs each have **zero** new rows. One DERIVED_FROM ImpactLink ties the new proof to profile. Contract fixtures must pass the actual immutable schema24 Artifact/ImpactLink/VersionRef schemas before Source acceptance.
24: 
25: ## Frozen plan and deterministic writes
26: 
27: Preflight allocates operation ID, proof Artifact ID, upload key, ImpactLink ID and EventEnvelope ID, a current observation timestamp and bounded expiry. PlanCore freezes native root/database identity, schema fingerprint, contracts hashes, all input/authority/body hashes, those IDs/times, expected event sequence and target subject. `plan_hash = SHA256(canonical PlanCore)`; proof embeds this hash. A FullPlan then contains PlanCore, exact proof bytes and planned output rows; its raw file digest is `plan_file_sha256`. Idempotency request_hash uses plan_file_sha256. There is no self-referential proof/full-plan hash. Current identity/time are checked at preflight and commit; changed inputs require a new reviewed plan. No materialized default Now()/ID() may silently change frozen rows at commit.
28: 
29: Use a new transaction-only planned writer in qualification_failure_maintenance_windows.go. It rechecks the same author, reference access, byte hash/size, unique artifact content and provenance invariants as upload+seal, inserts the planned upload, calls existing `s.put` for planned Artifact/ImpactLink/Run/ProjectState/EventEnvelope, and sets upload sealed in that transaction. Construct ImpactLink with existing semantics (validate both versions; ACTIVE/DERIVED_FROM/DETERMINISTIC/evidence_refs=[]). Use a planned event helper with the exact semantics of store.go:event, but explicit IDs/timestamp and no internal commit. This avoids reusing random-ID helpers or adding a broad clock injection. Schema validation and `s.put` still enforce all ordinary entity/revision/reference invariants. No raw generic SQL endpoint or blanket helper bypass is added.
30: 
31: The exact C v1 subject must already have old result_artifact_ids matching its original native output manifest byte-for-byte, or both must be empty. A historical unimported output requires a separately expanded scope; this package does not import REPORT outputs as an incidental repair. Preserve checkpoint pointer and validate any existing pointer; no new checkpoint.
32: 
33: The schema24 transaction uses one existing DB connection and one transaction with a proven SQLite write reservation. Revalidate full schema and before census, all CAS subjects, current Owner/Host/root and immutable evidence. No constructor that calls store.Open migrations, Service.New/NewCurrentMu, Host.New bootstrap, provider/vault/coordinator or listeners is allowed. New store helper opens existing `mode=rw`, refuses absent DB/URI aliases, validates WAL/FULL/foreign-key settings on this maintenance connection and exact schema fingerprint (sqlite_master tables, indexes, triggers/views + migration rows + contracts hashes), and takes the reservation before CAS. Source must prove its transaction primitive is compatible with the tx-aware domain writers; no nested BEGIN/implicit helper transaction.
38: 
39: | Table | Exact rows/fields allowed |
40: |---|---|
41: | domain_objects | UPDATE current Run and current ProjectState only; INSERT one Artifact, one ImpactLink, one EventEnvelope. No old object delete. |
42: | domain_versions | INSERT exactly five versions: Run r+1, ProjectState p+1, Artifact1, ImpactLink1, EventEnvelope1. Old versions byte-identical. |
43: | domain_refs | INSERT precisely the references generated by these five frozen bodies; enumerate project/kind/id/revision/field/target tuple in FullPlan. No old ref changes. |
44: | uploaded_content | INSERT one planned upload key, current Owner principal, exact proof bytes/content_hash/size-derived body, frozen expires_at; sealed final1. No old content changes. |
45: | runtime_observations | INSERT one (project,run,epoch,receipt_hash=Hash(derived observation)) with exact canonical body and frozen observed_at. |
46: | runtime_dispatches | UPDATE exactly (project,run,epoch): state OBSERVED, observation_sequence=max(original bridge sequence,stored observation_sequence)+1, observation_hash, updated_at and a deterministic reconstruction reason. Identity/manifest/manifest_hash/dispatch_key/worker/locator/prepared_at unchanged. |
47: | outbox | INSERT one (project,sequence,id), body identical to new EventEnvelope, acknowledged0. No old acknowledgement edits. |
48: | event_state_snapshots | INSERT one (project,event_id,revision=ProjectState p+1,body=exact updated ProjectState). |
49: | idempotency | INSERT one (principal=currentOwner,project,operation=`host:qualification-failure-maintenance`,key=operationID), request_hash=plan_file_sha256,status200,headers={},created_at=frozen time, body={schema,operation_id,plan_hash,plan_file_sha256,subject,proof_ref,observation_hash,terminal_run_ref,outcome_hash}. |
50: | runtime_uploads / artifact_uses / artifact_use_proofs | ZERO rows: current maintenance proof has run_id=null. |
